# Ship NOTHING into the build context except what the Dockerfile uses.
# The build references exactly two files (docker-entrypoint.sh, COPYed, and
# scripts/apk-purge.sh, bind-mounted for one RUN and never stored); deny-all then
# re-allow keeps the context to a few KB and makes it impossible for a stray
# `COPY .`/`ADD` to bake .git, secrets, SBOMs, or IDE state into an image layer.
*
!docker-entrypoint.sh
!scripts/apk-purge.sh
